{% comment %}
  Renders the cart drawer's cross-sell rail.

  Every line in the cart is looked up in the merchandising sheet (see
  'cart-recommendation-map'). Each match is rotated by a time-based offset so the rail is not
  frozen on the same handful of products, then the matched lists are interleaved round-robin
  so every product in the cart gets a slot rather than the first line filling all of them.
  Anything already in the cart is dropped, since there is nothing to cross-sell there.

  Falls back to the collection picked in theme settings whenever the cart is empty, nothing
  in it appears in the sheet, or every candidate was filtered out -- that fallback is the
  behaviour the rail had before it was made per-product.

  Accepts:
  - animate_delay: {Number} data-animate-delay-N bucket for the drawer's entrance animation

  Usage:
  {% render 'cart-recommendations', animate_delay: 6 %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign recommendations_limit = 8

  comment
    all_products is capped at 20 unique lookups per render and 'free-gift' spends some of
    that budget, so candidates are resolved lazily and abandoned once this many have been
    tried. Anything past the cap would return blank and drop out of the rail anyway.
  endcomment
  assign lookup_budget = 16

  capture recommendation_map
    render 'cart-recommendation-map'
  endcapture
  assign map_rows = recommendation_map | split: ';'

  comment
    Handles already in the cart, wrapped in commas on both sides so `contains` cannot match
    a handle that merely starts with another one.
  endcomment
  assign handles_in_cart = ','
  for item in cart.items
    assign handles_in_cart = handles_in_cart | append: item.product.handle | append: ','
  endfor

  comment
    The rotation seed is derived from which products are in the cart, never from the clock.
    The drawer re-fetches this section on every cart:refresh and swaps in the new innerHTML,
    so a seed that moved between renders would visibly reshuffle the rail a network
    round-trip after the drawer opens. Same cart, same markup, nothing moves.

    Quantities are deliberately left out: bumping a quantity should not reorder the rail.
    Adding or removing a product does change the seed, but the recommendations legitimately
    change at that point anyway.
  endcomment
  assign shuffle_seed = 0
  for item in cart.items
    assign line_signature = item.variant.id | modulo: 997
    assign shuffle_seed = shuffle_seed | plus: line_signature
  endfor

  comment
    One rotated cross-sell list per matching cart line: lists separated by '|', handles by '~'.
  endcomment
  assign matched_lists = ''

  for item in cart.items
    assign variant_key = item.product.handle | append: '?variant=' | append: item.variant.id
    assign variant_match = ''
    assign handle_match = ''

    for row in map_rows
      assign row_parts = row | split: '>>'
      if row_parts.size < 2
        continue
      endif
      assign row_key = row_parts[0] | strip
      if row_key == variant_key
        assign variant_match = row_parts[1]
        break
      elsif row_key == item.product.handle
        assign handle_match = row_parts[1]
      endif
    endfor

    comment
      A row keyed to this exact variant beats the row keyed to the bare handle, which is how
      the mini sizes get their own cross-sells.
    endcomment
    assign matched = handle_match
    if variant_match != blank
      assign matched = variant_match
    endif
    if matched == blank
      continue
    endif

    comment
      Rotating keeps every cart from leading with the same product; offsetting by the line's
      position keeps two cart lines from rotating in lockstep.
    endcomment
    assign recs = matched | split: ','
    assign rotate_by = shuffle_seed | plus: forloop.index0 | modulo: recs.size
    assign last_position = recs.size | minus: 1
    assign rotated = ''
    for position in (0..last_position)
      assign pick = position | plus: rotate_by | modulo: recs.size
      assign rec_entry = recs[pick] | strip
      assign rotated = rotated | append: rec_entry | append: '~'
    endfor

    assign matched_lists = matched_lists | append: rotated | append: '|'
  endfor

  comment
    Round-robin the lists together: first pick from every cart line, then second pick from
    every cart line, and so on. Eight passes covers the longest row in the sheet; the size
    guard makes any extra pass a no-op if a longer row is ever added.
  endcomment
  assign per_line_lists = matched_lists | split: '|'
  assign interleaved = ''
  for pass in (0..7)
    for line_list in per_line_lists
      assign line_entries = line_list | split: '~'
      if pass < line_entries.size
        assign interleaved = interleaved | append: line_entries[pass] | append: '~'
      endif
    endfor
  endfor

  comment
    Walk the merged order and keep the first `recommendations_limit` products that are not
    already in the cart, not already picked, and actually purchasable right now.
  endcomment
  assign candidates = interleaved | split: '~'
  assign chosen = ''
  assign chosen_count = 0
  assign lookups_used = 0
  assign seen_handles = ','

  for candidate in candidates
    if chosen_count >= recommendations_limit or lookups_used >= lookup_budget
      break
    endif

    assign candidate_handle = candidate | split: '?' | first
    assign candidate_marker = candidate_handle | prepend: ',' | append: ','
    if handles_in_cart contains candidate_marker
      continue
    endif
    if seen_handles contains candidate_marker
      continue
    endif
    assign seen_handles = seen_handles | append: candidate_handle | append: ','

    assign lookups_used = lookups_used | plus: 1
    assign candidate_product = all_products[candidate_handle]
    unless candidate_product.available
      continue
    endunless

    assign chosen = chosen | append: candidate | append: '~'
    assign chosen_count = chosen_count | plus: 1
  endfor

  assign chosen_entries = chosen | split: '~'

  assign fallback_products = settings.cart_recommendations_collection.products
  assign show_recommendations = true
  if chosen_entries.size == 0
    if settings.cart_recommendations_collection == blank or fallback_products.size == 0
      assign show_recommendations = false
    endif
  endif
-%}

{%- if show_recommendations -%}
  <cart-recommendations
    class="cart-card cart-recommendations"
    {% if animate_delay %}data-animate data-animate-delay-{{ animate_delay }}{% endif %}
  >
    <p class="cart-card__title">{{ settings.cart_recommendations_heading | escape }}</p>
    <ul class="cart-recommendations__list list-unstyled">
      {%- if chosen_entries.size > 0 -%}
        {%- for entry in chosen_entries -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign entry_handle = entry | split: '?' | first
            assign entry_variant_id = ''
            if entry contains '?variant='
              assign entry_variant_id = entry | split: '?variant=' | last
            endif
          -%}
          {% render 'cart-recommendation-card',
            recommendation: all_products[entry_handle],
            variant_id: entry_variant_id
          %}
        {%- endfor -%}
      {%- else -%}
        {%- for recommendation in fallback_products limit: recommendations_limit -%}
          {% render 'cart-recommendation-card', recommendation: recommendation %}
        {%- endfor -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    </ul>
  </cart-recommendations>
{%- endif -%}
